  "generated_text": "To find the other number, we can use the relationship between the least common multiple (LCM) and the greatest common divisor (GCD) of two numbers. The relationship is given by the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{LCM} \\times \\text{GCD} = \\text{Product of the two numbers}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n- LCM = 3780\n- GCD = 18\n- One number = 180\n\nLet the other number be \\( x \\).\n\nUsing the relationship:\n\\[\n3780 \\times 18 = 180 \\times x\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate the product on the left side:\n\\[\n3780 \\times 18 = 68040\n\\]\n\nSo, the equation becomes:\n\\[\n68040 = 180x\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( x \\), divide both sides by 180:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{68040}{180} = 378\n\\]\n\nThus, the other number is \\(\\boxed{378}\\).",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[378, '378']",
    "gold_answer": "We use the identity $\\gcd(a,b) \\cdot \\mathop{\\text{lcm}}[a,b] = ab$ for all positive integers $a$ and $b$.  We are told that $\\gcd(a,b) = 18$, and $\\mathop{\\text{lcm}}[a,b] = 3780$, so $ab = 18 \\cdot 3780$.  If one number is 180, then the other number is $18 \\cdot 3780/180 = \\boxed{378}$.",
    "is_correct": true
  },
